<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Wired at step P4 of docs/ios-appstore-release.md (paid team, 2026-10-06). Every capability ships
  DORMANT and switches on from the server, with no new binary:
  - Universal links answer only once eno.vn serves /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, which
    needs APPLE_TEAM_ID in eno-vn.env (step P7). Until then iOS finds no association and links
    keep opening Safari.
  - aps-environment lets native push work once APNs is configured and NEXT_PUBLIC_NATIVE_PUSH_IOS=1
    is set (step P8). Xcode re-signs it as `production` when the archive is exported for App Store
    Connect.
  - Sign in with Apple (build 3 of 1.0.3 on; SIWA plan 2026-10-08, decision D1, which replaces the
    v1 decision D2 = b): com.apple.developer.applesignin = [Default] is what lets the native Apple
    sheet in EnoSignInPlugin.swift run. The site shows Apple, and Google beside it (Guideline 4.8),
    only once NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SIGNIN carries `ios` (src/lib/apple-signin.ts); until then this
    binary offers the email code only, exactly like build 2. Automatic signing can issue a profile
    with it only once App ID vn.eno.app has Sign in with Apple enabled as a PRIMARY App ID (SIWA plan
    owner step 2; the web Services ID is grouped under it). scripts/ios-release.sh refuses an
    archive that does not carry exactly [Default].
  ⛔ applinks:eno.vn AND NOTHING ELSE (owner, 2026-10-06: "ship both with eno.vn"). The app renders
  the licensed marketplace and its company is the App Store seller, so eno.vn is the domain that
  vouches for it. NEVER an eno.forum host: the forum carries the services the licensed company may
  not offer, and a claimed forum link would open this app instead of the browser. A claim in a
  submitted binary can only be withdrawn by another submission; scripts/ios-release.sh refuses any
  other set. www.eno.vn 308s to the apex for every path, the association file included, so it could
  never be listed anyway.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:eno.vn</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
